From: PwndaWallet <pwndamining@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] basicswap: register the Zephyr (ZEPH) coin module in
 the shared engine files

Wires the four new files from PWNDA-PATCH-13 (basicswap/interface/zephyr/)
into the engine so it actually constructs a ZEPHInterface and provisions it,
on the shared files this tree's upstream #532 refactor centralised:
basicswap/chainparams.py (the Coins enum id + the two coin-family tuples +
the chainparams dict), basicswap/basicswap.py (createInterface + the
thread_func poll-loop map), basicswap/bin/prepare.py (coin_prepare_modules +
known_coins + the chainclients config-segment dict), basicswap/bin/run.py
(the native, non-Docker daemon/wallet-rpc start path), and
basicswap/ui/page_settings.py (the two xmr-family coin-name tuples the
Settings page's read/write handlers gate on).

Modelled directly on the existing Coins.WOW registration at every site below
-- WOW is the nearest sibling (also a Monero-fork xmr_based_coins member on
this per-coin-folder layout) and every hunk here is "add ZEPH next to WOW",
never a new pattern. Authoritative shape confirmed against
ResearchWiki/synthesis/zeph-coin-add-dev-restructure-replan.md ("Phase 2 -
central registrations") in G:\REU26 (read-only reference, not part of this
tree), which re-ported this exact registration onto this exact per-coin-
folder layout and validated it live (`basicswap-prepare --withcoins=zephyr
--preparebinonly` ran the new core.py end to end; `test_other` green; CI-
pinned lint clean). Two things follow that page's own recorded lesson rather
than its older draft: no inline-tuple edits to basicswap.py's
scriptless_coins/xmr_based_coins are made here, because this tree's dev base
(post upstream #543) already centralises both tuples into chainparams.py as
single-source-of-truth imports -- basicswap.py's own copies were dropped
upstream, exactly the "delete our duplicate, extend dev's tuple" lesson the
replan's 2026-07-13 entry records after hitting the equivalent conflict
itself. Confirmed by grep against this tree: only two `Coins.WOW` sites exist
in the entirety of basicswap.py (createInterface, thread_func) -- both
patched below, nothing else references it.

Three additions the replan's Phase 2 section does not itself enumerate,
found by tracing this patch's own gate command through prepare.py's actual
control flow rather than assumed from the replan text alone (the replan's
own validation used --preparebinonly, a different code path that never
reaches these three):
  - bin/prepare.py's `known_coins` dict needs a "zephyr" entry, because
    `--withcoins=zephyr` is parsed through `ensure_coin_valid()`, which
    exits immediately with "Unknown coin Zephyr" if the name is absent from
    `known_coins` -- before `coin_prepare_modules` is ever consulted at all.
  - bin/prepare.py's `chainclients` dict (built once, unconditionally, right
    where "monero"/"wownero" call their own `getConfigSegment(prepare_ctx)`)
    needs a "zephyr" entry too: this is literally the dict this patch's own
    gate checks for a `chainclients.zephyr` block in, and it is populated
    independently of `coin_prepare_modules` -- omitting it would leave
    `--withcoins=zephyr` parse successfully, `known_coins["zephyr"]` resolve
    fine, and `settings["chainclients"]` still come up short one key,
    silently.
  - bin/run.py's `if c in ("monero", "wownero"):` dispatch (the ONLY place
    that gates which coins get routed through the shared `startXmrDaemon`
    / `startXmrWalletDaemon` functions at all -- those two functions
    themselves have no coin gate of their own) needs "zephyr" added, so a
    native (non-Docker) Grove install can start a local ZEPH daemon/wallet-
    rpc exactly the way it already starts Monero's. Grove's own core.py
    (PWNDA-PATCH-13) hardcodes manage_daemon/manage_wallet_daemon to False
    for ZEPH -- this dispatch branch is therefore dead code in Grove's own
    default deployment (ZEPH is always the C-RZ remote/host-leased wallet)
    -- but it is the exact gap unit A4 (Phase A) had to build a standalone
    regtest harness around instead of using run.py directly, and closing it
    here, in the engine's own native-start path, is this patch's job per
    the Grove expansion master plan's Phase B table, not a follow-up left
    for whoever eventually needs a locally-managed ZEPH node.

A real defect found and fixed WHILE building this patch, not merely
inherited: `startXmrDaemon`'s `config_filename` ternary and
`startXmrWalletDaemon`'s `wallet_config_filename` ternary look like the same
pattern (both keyed on the binary name's prefix, both currently special-
casing only "wow") but they are NOT symmetric on the provisioning side, and
treating them as symmetric here would have shipped a second, silent
mismatch alongside PWNDA-PATCH-13's own already-documented one. Traced by
actually running this patch's own gate end to end (see below) and reading
the real `basicswap.json` + datadir it produced, not by inspecting the two
ternaries in isolation:
  - The DAEMON conf name (`prepareDataDir`'s
    `core_settings.get("config_filename", self.name + "d.conf")`, in
    `basicswap/interface/prepare_util.py`'s base `CoinPrepareModule`) is
    NAME-DERIVED by default, and ZEPHPrepare (PWNDA-PATCH-13) sets no
    `config_filename` override, so the real file `basicswap-prepare` writes
    to a zephyr datadir is `zephyrd.conf` -- exactly what
    `daemon_bin.startswith("zephyr")` needed to produce. This branch is
    correct and necessary; verified live (see gate output).
  - The WALLET conf name is the opposite shape: `XMRPrepare.
    getWalletConfFilename()` (`basicswap/interface/xmr/core.py`) hardcodes
    the literal string `"monero_wallet.conf"` -- it is NOT derived from
    `self.name` the way the daemon conf is. WOWPrepare overrides this
    method (`basicswap/interface/wow/core.py`) to return its own name;
    ZEPHPrepare (PWNDA-PATCH-13) does not override it at all, so it
    inherits the literal `"monero_wallet.conf"` default -- confirmed by
    running this patch's own gate and reading the resulting zephyr datadir,
    which contains a real file named `monero_wallet.conf`, never
    `zephyr-wallet-rpc.conf`. An earlier draft of this patch added a
    "zephyr" branch to `wallet_config_filename` pointing at
    `zephyr-wallet-rpc.conf` (mirroring the daemon-conf ternary by
    reflex); running the gate against it would have looked identical
    (`--nocores` never reaches `startXmrWalletDaemon` at all), so this
    defect would have shipped invisibly -- the actual file
    `startXmrWalletDaemon` would have gone looking for
    `zephyr-wallet-rpc.conf`, found nothing (`os.path.exists(config_path)`
    false), and started the wallet-rpc daemon with NO config file at all:
    no `--rpc-bind-port`, no `--wallet-dir`, no `--rpc-login`, in a native
    (non-Docker) install with `manage_wallet_daemon` ever flipped True by
    hand. Caught only because this patch's gate reads the actual datadir
    produced, not just the process exit code. FIX: `wallet_config_filename`
    is left untouched by this patch -- "zephyr-wallet-rpc" already falls
    through the existing `else "monero_wallet.conf"` branch unchanged,
    which is the file that actually gets written, so no ternary edit was
    needed there at all. Filed as a defect below and cross-referenced for
    B-INT / a future PWNDA-PATCH-13 follow-up: ZEPHPrepare could override
    `getWalletConfFilename()` for cosmetic self-consistency with WOW, but
    it is not a functional bug as things stand -- each coin's conf lives in
    its own isolated datadir, so the literal "monero_wallet.conf" name
    never collides with an actual Monero installation's own file.

Two deliberate omissions, both because Grove never manages a local ZEPH
daemon (see the point above -- the same reasoning PWNDA-PATCH-13's core.py
already gives for hardcoding manage_daemon/manage_wallet_daemon False), so
neither line has anything to do at runtime for this project:
  - bin/prepare.py's per-coin `--<name>restoreheight=N` CLI flag and its
    `chainclients["<name>"]["restore_height"] = <name>_restore_height` /
    `["trusted_daemon"] = extra_opts.get(...)` follow-up assignment (present
    for "monero" and "wownero" only, not generalised to every xmr-family
    coin already in this tree -- FIRO and DOGE get no equivalent override
    either). ZEPHPrepare.getConfigSegment (PWNDA-PATCH-13) already sets its
    own restore_height default; a CLI override to reach a daemon Grove never
    manages would be unreachable code, not a real capability.
  - bin/prepare.py's `electrum_supported_coins` dict (`{"bitcoin": "btc",
    "litecoin": "ltc"}`) -- ZEPH is a Monero-fork RPC coin, not an
    electrum-protocol coin; unrelated to this patch's coin family entirely
    (that dict is BCH/BTC/LTC's concern, PWNDA-PATCH-18).

Checked and confirmed NO changes needed (so not touched, per the replan's
own 2026-07-13 finding that dev's refactor already generalised these two
files to iterate xmr_based_coins/chainparams rather than hardcode per-coin
tuples): basicswap/ui/page_offers.py, basicswap/ui/page_wallet.py -- grepped
for "wownero"/"monero" tuples in both; zero matches in this tree, matching
what the replan page itself records happened on dev after upstream #543.
basicswap/interface/electrumx.py and basicswap/bin/prepare.py's
`electrum_supported_coins` dict are PWNDA-PATCH-18's (BCH) files, not
touched here.

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.5 (3859612035f8c4476b5cadedf36b875d2f2def5b),
after PWNDA-PATCH-13 (basicswap/interface/zephyr/ must exist first).
